---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import data from '../data/scholarships.json';
import { formatDate } from '../lib/scholarships';
---

<Base
  title="About and sources"
  description="How FreeStudentKit works, how scholarship information is checked, and the limits of the tools."
>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">About and sources</h1>
  <div class="prose-fsk mt-4 max-w-2xl space-y-4">
    <p>
      FreeStudentKit is a free set of tools and checked information for Nigerian students. It has no accounts and no adverts,
      and your CGPA, semesters and invoices stay on your own device.
    </p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">How scholarships are checked</h2>
    <p>
      Each scholarship is traced to its provider's official page or an official Nigerian government notice where one exists.
      When only news articles or school notices were available, the entry says “Reported”. When sources disagree, it says
      “Check before applying”. Dates and eligibility are summaries, so always confirm on the official page. The list was last
      checked on {formatDate(data.checkedOn)}.
    </p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Limits of the tools</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
      <li>Degree class bands and grading scales differ between schools. The CGPA tool uses typical values, so check yours.</li>
      <li>The GPA converter and aggregate calculator give estimates. Use your school's official figures for anything formal.</li>
      <li>Project topics are starting ideas, not finished projects. Agree your final topic with your supervisor.</li>
      <li>Citation output follows the main rules of each style. Check it against your department's guide.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Scams</h2>
    <p>Genuine scholarships and loans do not charge application fees. Do not send money to anyone who offers to “secure” a place for you.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
